  "body": "fix(post): refuse a left-hand cutter on posts that cannot reverse the spindle\n\n#4031, steps 1, 2 and 5 (the maintainer scoped the work; steps 3 and 4\nare the follow-up #4102).\n\nWhat changed:\n- `Tool` gains `cutter_hand` (`crates/tools::CutterHand`, right by\n  default), separate from the tap's `thread_hand` - a left-hand tap cuts\n  a left thread while its spindle may still turn right. The catalog\n  reader, the project file, the MCP `tool_edit` and the tool editor\n  carry the field; the UI shows a \"Left-hand cutter (spindle reverse,\n  M4)\" row for every kind that turns a spindle.\n- The tool gate refuses a left-hand cutter by name for every operation\n  whose setup posts through a built-in post that starts a spindle M3 and\n  never reverses it (Haas, Tormach PathPilot, Doosan DNM, Grbl 1.1,\n  grblHAL, Makera Carvera, Heidenhain, Heidenhain Klartext): at creation\n  (`tool_refusal`) and as an operation's after-state (`tool_problem`),\n  so generation, the post, the tree and the page all say the same\n  sentence. A post that reverses (Fanuc, Mazak, Mach4, Siemens 810M)\n  keeps a left-hand cutter offered; a post of the user's own stays open.\n- A left-hand cutter rides the generation digest (`stamp_tool`), so a\n  tool edited to left-hand marks its operations stale.\n- Versions: the project file steps to v83 (a v82 reader would silently\n  drop the hand and post M3) and a `.camtools` library with a left-hand\n  cutter steps to `CUTTER_HAND_VERSION` 7 (accepted: 1..=7).\n\nReadings: the M3-only list is the maintainer's step-2 list; the\npost-side reverse path exists since #988 (`ask_reverse_spindle` + the\n`millSpindleReverse` manifest flag), which steps 3 and 4 (#4102) will\nread.\n\nRework (mkinney's review of 8f0cc012, commits 73a142e92 + 98ec365db):\n- The law reads the REQUEST, not the post (#4031 rework): a left-hand\n  cutter is allowed only for an operation that asks the spindle to\n  reverse - today only a Thread operation with spindle reverse, the one\n  path that calls `ask_reverse_spindle` and posts M4 - and still\n  refused on the M3-only posts even then. A permitted post reverses\n  nothing on its own; a user post file is judged by the same request.\n  Every other kind - Drill, Face, Contour, Pocket, Adaptive, Bore,\n  Circular and every multiaxis kind - refuses the left hand by name\n  until #4102 lands. A left-hand cutter posts M4 or meets a named\n  refusal; it never posts M3.\n- Output tests: the Thread op with the ask posts M4 through the Fanuc\n  post; the whole catalog table of kinds refuses the left hand without\n  the ask; a left-hand Drill refuses at creation and at generation and\n  post on the reversing Fanuc as much as on Haas, and no NC file is\n  written.\n- The example `examples/first-continuous-4axis-part.camproj` was\n  regenerated at v83 through the WRITE_GOLDEN save path. Moved goldens:\n  that project file only (its `\"version\"` row 82 -> 83; the committed\n  posted program is byte-identical).\n- The library-version boundary test refuses `CUTTER_HAND_VERSION + 1`\n  (version 8, the new newest) instead of `TIP_FORM_VERSION + 1`.\n- The project file's v83 step is a compatibility break; the ladder\n  comment names it and the breaking metadata rides commit 98ec365db.\n\nPinning tests:\n- `crates/app/tests/cutter_hand.rs` (new): the tool JSON round trip and\n  the unknown-hand refusal; the creation door refuses by name on each of\n  the eight M3-only posts; a left-hand Drill refuses even on the\n  reversing built-in Fanuc post; a Thread operation that asks to reverse\n  posts M4 with the left-hand mill; every kind without the reverse\n  request refuses the left hand by name; an edit to left-hand refuses\n  generation and post by name (no NC file written); the project round\n  trip; the library steps to version 7 only when a left-hand cutter is\n  present.\n- `crates/tools/tests/cutter_hand.rs` (new): the catalog reader keeps a\n  left hand, defaults legacy tools to right, and refuses a bad hand by\n  tool and field name. (New top-level test binaries, one per crate,\n  because each mirrors an existing issue binary - `tap_hand.rs` - that\n  stays a separate suite.)\n- `crates/app/tests/tool_library.rs`: the newer-number refusal moved\n  past version 7.\n- `crates/app/tests/tool_law.rs`, `holder_reference.rs`,\n  `continuous_4axis_part.rs`, `tap_hand.rs` and the `crates/motion` and\n  `crates/ui` suites that seed the field: green.\n\nGate on the rework head 98ec365db: `cutter_hand` 7 passed,\n`continuous_4axis_part` 10 passed, `holder_reference` 7 passed,\n`tool_library` 25 passed, `tool_law` 7 passed, `camcraft-ui --lib`\n1,688 passed, clippy `camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n\nNot exercised: steps 3 and 4 (#4102) - the posted-G-code proof of the\nallow side is today the Thread op's M4; every other kind refuses. The\nplasma, wire, sinker and waterjet posts touch no spindle and read no\nhand.\n\nHeavy step (P1 under the safety floor): `app heavy: tool_library`, ok on\nthe reviewed head 8f0cc012; its diff is untouched by the rework.\n\nChangelog: A tool states its cutter hand; a left-hand cutter posts M4\nonly where the operation asks to reverse, and is refused by name\neverywhere else - never posted under M3.\n\nScreenshots:\n- Before (the new-tool draft, no hand row):\n  https://github.com/FlamingFireCoding/Camcraft/blob/pr-screenshots/pr4103-tool-hand-before.png\n- After (the \"Left-hand cutter (spindle reverse, M4)\" row, 4x crop):\n  https://github.com/FlamingFireCoding/Camcraft/blob/pr-screenshots/pr4103-tool-hand-after.png\n\nFixes #4031\n",
